// =============================================================================
// taxes-records-course — "Taxes and Records: What You Owe and What You Can Show"
// =============================================================================
// Course eight of the Real Estate department. Seven courses covered the ground,
// the stewardship, the transaction, the tenant, the building, the partner and
// the lender. This one covers the two things that outlast all of them: what the
// authorities take, and what you can prove.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. Render unto Caesar (Matthew 22:17, 18, 19, 20, 21)
//   2. Then are the children free (Matthew 17:24, 25, 26, 27)
//   3. All the world should be taxed (Luke 2:1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
//   4. The rich shall not give more (Exodus 30:12, 13, 15, 16)
//   5. He will take the tenth (1 Samuel 8:11, 14, 15, 17, 18)
//   6. They sought their register (Ezra 2:59, 62, 63)
//   7. The principal and the fifth part (Leviticus 6:2, 5)
//   8. Will a man rob God (Malachi 3:8, 9, 10)
//
// Settle that two claims exist -> learn that being right and insisting are two
// decisions -> see that the record is not outside His government -> get a
// standard for judging a levy that is not its rate -> assemble the total you
// have never seen -> find out what you cannot produce -> fix what you found
// yourself, at a price -> and end on the one account with no examiner.
//
// WHY LESSON 8 IS LAST. The first seven obligations all carry an EXTERNAL
// instrument of measurement: a notice, a bill, an amortisation schedule, a
// party who asks to see the document. The eighth has none, which is why the
// nation in Malachi 3 asked "Wherein have we robbed thee?" sincerely. The
// course is built so that question lands after seven sessions of measuring
// everything else.
//
// THE LINE THIS COURSE HOLDS (DR-0098). Lesson 4 is the one most likely to be
// pressed into service as a tax-policy argument, so it states its own limit in
// the text: a census offering with an atonement purpose is not a revenue
// platform, and reading it as one reads past what it says. Lesson 5 is the one
// most likely to scold a reader for burdens he never chose, so it ends by
// splitting the schedule into what was consented to and what was added after
// commitment. Lesson 8 refuses both abuses of Malachi 3:10 by name.
//
// THE DEPARTMENT'S RECURRING SHAPE, a ninth time: a defect invisible from
// inside any single instance. Twelve reasonable assessments in twelve separate
// envelopes, each one read and paid, that have never been added up; and a
// register nobody thought to write down because everybody already knew.
//
// NO PASSAGE IS SHARED with any of the department's other seven courses, and
// the course test CHECKS that against their own reference lists. All eight
// book-and-chapters are fresh against the 81 already in use.
//
// BANDS, BENEFITS AND STORIES FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0509). Every lesson
// carries levels.teen and levels.senior (DR-0497/0498), six `benefits`, and two
// `stories`, so neither the send stage nor the teach stage can render a heading
// with nothing under it.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). All 137 quoted spans
// fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV. The generator caught seven
// spans in the first draft that had dropped a POSSESSIVE APOSTROPHE -- Caesar's,
// God's, their father's house -- because the author was avoiding a straight
// quote inside a JS string. A quotation missing an apostrophe is not verbatim,
// and the fix is the typographic apostrophe the generator normalises, not a
// shorter span. Our prose says Yahweh; quotations keep "God" and "the LORD"
// exactly as the KJV has them (DR-0210's bright line).
//
// TEACHING, NOT TAX OR LEGAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta. Assessment methods,
// appeal deadlines, exemptions, deductibility, basis and record-retention
// periods are jurisdiction specific and they change.
// =============================================================================

